clean_summary:
We have a winner of the Lenny's Newsletter x @Replit buildathon. Congratulations to @andrey_esipov for creating Operators, a Street Fighter II-inspired fighting game where each fighter is an operator from Lenny's Podcast. Each special move corresponds to a framework discussed on the show, linked to the episode and timestamp.

The project showcases a lot of craftsmanship and personality, and the team enjoyed testing it. Several other projects came close, including Little Lenny's, Lenny's Diner, LennyOS, Oracle of Lenny, and Pod-Squad. Thanks to everyone who entered; more AI-building fun is coming.

@lennysan announced the buildathon, encouraging participants to create with podcast and newsletter data on Replit for prizes like coaching, credits, and a free year of Lenny's Newsletter. The first 200 joiners also get a free month of Replit Core.

You can now build with Replit and deploy straight to Microsoft Fabric. Code is the easy part; the backend—identities, storage, schemas, governance—is the hard part. You build in Replit, and the app and data deploy into your enterprise-managed Microsoft Fabric tenant.

Microsoft CEO Satya Nadella announced this in his Microsoft Build 2026 opening keynote.

@Replit: "Announcing our new collaboration with @Microsoft. Organizations can now build internal tools, workflows, or data dashboards in Replit and publish directly to Microsoft Fabric with security, authentication, and governance built in."

Interactive AI movie site built in Replit features three short films created entirely with AI video generation and vibe coding. Powered by Flora AI and Kling AI, it offers an immersive experience about direction in the AI era.

